{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2019-12-17 22:30:00', 'title': 'PG&E SAYS SUBMITS COMPREHENSIVE, MULTI-PARTY SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT TO CPUC RELATED TO 2017, 2018 WILDFIRES', 'text': 'PG&E SUBMITS COMPREHENSIVE, MULTI-PARTY SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT TO CPUC RELATED TO 2017 AND 2018 WILDFIRES.SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT PROHIBITS COMPANY FROM SEEKING $1.625 BILLION IN WILDFIRE-RELATED COSTS FROM CUSTOMERS.PROPOSES PG&E SHAREHOLDER-FUNDED PAYMENTS OF $50 MILLION FOR SYSTEM ENHANCEMENTS.SETTLEMENT ALSO PROPOSES THAT PG&E NOT SEEK CUSTOMER RATE RECOVERY ASSOCIATED WITH CERTAIN WILDFIRE-RELATED COSTS IN AMOUNT OF $1.625 BILLION.'}{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2019-12-17 02:30:00', 'title': 'PG&E SAYS ENTERED INTO AN AMENDMENT TO RESTRUCTURING SUPPORT AGREEMENT WITH INDIVIDUAL WILDFIRE VICTIMS’ REPRESENTATIVES', 'text': 'PG&E ANNOUNCES AMENDMENT TO RESTRUCTURING SUPPORT AGREEMENT WITH INDIVIDUAL WILDFIRE VICTIMS’ REPRESENTATIVES.PARTIES INTEND TO PROCEED WITH TORT CLAIMANTS RSA APPROVAL HEARING BEFORE BANKRUPTCY COURT ON DECEMBER 17, 2019.INTENDS TO COMPLY WITH PROVISIONS OF AB 1054 & WILL CONTINUE TO ADDRESS CONCERNS IN LETTER TO COMPANY FROM GOVERNOR DATED DECEMBER 13, 2019.'}